[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/2914327699","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82#issuecomment-2914327699","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82","id":2914327699,"node_id":"IC_kwDON056nM6ttRyT","user":{"login":"connor4312","id":2230985,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMzA5ODU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2230985?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312","html_url":"https://github.com/connor4312","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"created_at":"2025-05-27T22:30:53Z","updated_at":"2025-05-27T22:31:13Z","body":"I had a request on this for VS Code. I didn't dive deep into it but there are a couple scenarios that complicate this.\n\n1. Servers that provide a dynamic tools\n2. Tools that localized (https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/pull/115)\n3. Tools that may change depending on the model (https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/issues/469)\n\nJust letting clients do this may make more sense because the client will know at least (2) and (3) or know when they change. But the ecosystem tooling here is still quite immature.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/2914327699/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/2914334229","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82#issuecomment-2914334229","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82","id":2914334229,"node_id":"IC_kwDON056nM6ttTYV","user":{"login":"tadasant","id":3900899,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDA4OTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3900899?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant","html_url":"https://github.com/tadasant","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-27T22:32:50Z","updated_at":"2025-05-27T22:32:50Z","body":"If we focus on the notion of _possible_ tools (i.e. any tool that could ever surface, beyond just at-initialization), those three problems go away, right?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/2914334229/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/2914339852","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82#issuecomment-2914339852","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82","id":2914339852,"node_id":"IC_kwDON056nM6ttUwM","user":{"login":"connor4312","id":2230985,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMzA5ODU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2230985?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312","html_url":"https://github.com/connor4312","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"created_at":"2025-05-27T22:34:37Z","updated_at":"2025-05-27T22:34:46Z","body":"Yes. It's a bit of a pain because, given both (2) and (3) happen it's a `NxM` multiplier to the number of tools, but it's possible.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/2914339852/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/2914341535","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82#issuecomment-2914341535","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82","id":2914341535,"node_id":"IC_kwDON056nM6ttVKf","user":{"login":"connor4312","id":2230985,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMzA5ODU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2230985?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312","html_url":"https://github.com/connor4312","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"created_at":"2025-05-27T22:35:48Z","updated_at":"2025-05-27T22:35:48Z","body":"(though practically only a relatively small number of servers will get localized into a large number of languages)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/2914341535/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/2923074251","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82#issuecomment-2923074251","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82","id":2923074251,"node_id":"IC_kwDON056nM6uOpLL","user":{"login":"connor4312","id":2230985,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMzA5ODU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2230985?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312","html_url":"https://github.com/connor4312","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"created_at":"2025-05-30T18:13:10Z","updated_at":"2025-05-30T18:13:10Z","body":"I think tool representation overall, either in the registry spec or MCP metadata, would be useful. Currently clients need to start servers in order to know what tools, prompts, etc. are available. Because MCP servers can now do nice authentication, this can lead to a bunch of login prompts for the user when they first start interacting with their language model. If servers optionally (there might always be servers with nondeterministic tools) published their starting set of tools/prompts, then we could avoid this.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/2923074251/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/2923410876","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82#issuecomment-2923410876","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82","id":2923410876,"node_id":"IC_kwDON056nM6uP7W8","user":{"login":"jonathanhefner","id":771968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3MTk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/771968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathanhefner","html_url":"https://github.com/jonathanhefner","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathanhefner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathanhefner/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathanhefner/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathanhefner/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathanhefner/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathanhefner/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathanhefner/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathanhefner/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathanhefner/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-30T20:25:20Z","updated_at":"2025-05-30T20:25:20Z","body":"> I think tool representation overall, either in the registry spec or MCP metadata, would be useful. Currently clients need to start servers in order to know what tools, prompts, etc. are available.\n\nAgreed, in particular for tool representation in MCP metadata.  Unrelated to tool poisoning, but it might allow clients to statically index tools for client-side tool search.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/2923410876/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/3120388231","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82#issuecomment-3120388231","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82","id":3120388231,"node_id":"IC_kwDON056nM65_ViH","user":{"login":"goncalossilva","id":102931,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMjkzMQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102931?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva","html_url":"https://github.com/goncalossilva","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-25T21:17:23Z","updated_at":"2025-07-25T21:17:23Z","body":"Hi everyone, I'm glad that @tadasant raised this.\n\nWe are facing a challenge that would also be solved by having easy access to the tools provided by each MCP server. In our case, we want to avoid forcing a user to authenticate to a service before we can even confirm it has the tools to solve their problem (via `tools/list`).\n\nCould the `server` schema within the registry API be augmented to include `tools`? This would allow a server operator to choose to list their tool schemas publicly as part of the discovery process.\n\nThere are several benefits to this, from improved user experience for cases like ours, to more accurate MCP server selection in case there is more than one for a particular service, not to mention improved transparency within the ecosystem.\n\nA nuanced “possible tools” angle makes sense considering dynamic cases as [@connor4312 pointed out](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82#issuecomment-2914327699). However, while we want to support all cases, we do want to optimize for the common case. And the majority of MCP servers does have a static list of tools.\n\nHappy to contribute further details on our use case or to take part in the discussion on the details.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/3120388231/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/3121970215","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82#issuecomment-3121970215","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82","id":3121970215,"node_id":"IC_kwDON056nM66FXwn","user":{"login":"tadasant","id":3900899,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDA4OTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3900899?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant","html_url":"https://github.com/tadasant","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-26T14:18:07Z","updated_at":"2025-07-26T14:18:07Z","body":"Thanks @goncalossilva ! I think it'd be reasonable for someone to take on adding a field for statically defined tools.\n\nFrom a guidance perspective, we could say `SHOULD enumerate all possible tools`.\n\nSteps to contribute:\n1. Update https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/blob/4f5e85b51073bc878949850a44bd66d42e2d59fa/docs/server-json/schema.json\n2. Update https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/blob/main/docs/server-json/registry-schema.json\n3. Update https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/blob/main/docs/server-registry-api/openapi.yaml\n4. Include examples in the adjacent files, update any code this impacts\n\nFor the first update, would expect to see a thoughtful canvassing of any other precedent out there for this feature. For example, Anthropic's DXT format is probably good precedent for this / maybe we should align with their shape for tools. And the team there would probably have an opinion on this as well cc @felixrieseberg","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/3121970215/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/3131521253","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82#issuecomment-3131521253","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82","id":3131521253,"node_id":"IC_kwDON056nM66pzjl","user":{"login":"rdimitrov","id":16540482,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTQwNDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16540482?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdimitrov","html_url":"https://github.com/rdimitrov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdimitrov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdimitrov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdimitrov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdimitrov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdimitrov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdimitrov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdimitrov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdimitrov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdimitrov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-29T09:28:30Z","updated_at":"2025-07-29T09:28:30Z","body":"Would we rely on the author of the MCP server to populate the list of tools? If so should there be a way to prove/validate these upon publishing? What I mean is this raises a concern that bad actors can populate this list intentionally in a wrongful way which may cause malicious results further down. I'm supportive of having the tool's list in advance, just raising that it would be nice if there's a way to guarantee its correctness upon publishing and/or consuming.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/3131521253/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/3132983157","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82#issuecomment-3132983157","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82","id":3132983157,"node_id":"IC_kwDON056nM66vYd1","user":{"login":"tadasant","id":3900899,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDA4OTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3900899?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant","html_url":"https://github.com/tadasant","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-29T15:12:02Z","updated_at":"2025-07-29T15:12:02Z","body":"I don't think we can pursue running servers and introspecting them - there is too much of a rabbit hole there. What do you do for remote servers? What do you do for auth gates? What do you do for dynamic lists that won't be present on initial startup? Not to mention the quagmire that is trying to get them to run at all in a unified way across all the possible package registries.\n\nWe should think through what exposure there might be and give guidance on \"how consumers should use this data\" accordingly. At the end of the day, I only expect consumers to use this data as a kind of search/filtering/documentation mechanism; it shouldn't be \"run\" in any way, so not even prompt injection should be a concern here (perhaps we should give guidance to not pull this data into inference for any reason).\n\n@goncalossilva can you share more about the nature of your intended use case to help guide this level of trust factor?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/3132983157/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/3134459472","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82#issuecomment-3134459472","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82","id":3134459472,"node_id":"IC_kwDON056nM661A5Q","user":{"login":"goncalossilva","id":102931,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMjkzMQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102931?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva","html_url":"https://github.com/goncalossilva","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-30T00:16:44Z","updated_at":"2025-07-30T00:16:44Z","body":"> Steps to contribute\n\nThanks for these! I'm happy to push these forward soon.\n\n> can you share more about the nature of your intended use case to help guide this level of trust factor?\n\nWe're exploring using LLMs to convert prompts into workflows with minimal manual work from the user. The [upcoming](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/development/roadmap#registry) MCP registry is a great start to help us discover available MCP servers we might want to use, but that's generally not enough. We also need to know which capabilities are available in each MCP server.\n\nWe could do this back and forth of first identifying relevant MCP servers, then handling authentication, and only _then_ listing tools and preparing the workflow. And for now, we plan to do exactly that. But we're concerned about the use case where it's only after all of that, including effort from the user themself, that we realize we don't have the right tools to carry out the job. Determining that before the user puts in any effort would be _much_ better UX.\n\nDoes this help?\n\n---\n\nFor what it's worth, I agree that having to _prove_ the list of tools is complex and I wouldn't consider it for a first version. Trust is paramount, but this documentation _would_ be authored by the MCP server authors themselves. Potentially even automated via the SDK, reducing the risk of even unintentional errors. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/3134459472/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/3136682915","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82#issuecomment-3136682915","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82","id":3136682915,"node_id":"IC_kwDON056nM669fuj","user":{"login":"tadasant","id":3900899,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDA4OTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3900899?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant","html_url":"https://github.com/tadasant","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-30T14:47:19Z","updated_at":"2025-07-30T14:47:19Z","body":"> Does this help?\n\nThat makes sense! And aligned with what I was expecting / I stand by my earlier thoughts.\n\n> Potentially even automated via the SDK, reducing the risk of even unintentional errors.\n\nCurious what exactly you mean by this?\n\n---\n\nThank you for jumping in on this!\n\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/3136682915/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/3140081718","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82#issuecomment-3140081718","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82","id":3140081718,"node_id":"IC_kwDON056nM67Kdg2","user":{"login":"goncalossilva","id":102931,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMjkzMQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102931?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva","html_url":"https://github.com/goncalossilva","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-31T13:57:51Z","updated_at":"2025-07-31T13:57:51Z","body":"> > Potentially even automated via the SDK, reducing the risk of even unintentional errors.\n> \n> Curious what exactly you mean by this?\n\nThis is something I still have to explore, but seeing how users of MCP's SDKs annotate their tools (e.g., `@mcp.prompt(title=\"Do something\")` in Python) it may be possible to automate creating the “manifest” of tools for the registry, so there is less manual work involved, and consequently, it becomes less error-prone.\n\n> Thank you for jumping in on this!\n\nMy pleasure! Let's see where this goes. I'm off next week but planning to take some of the steps above after I'm back.\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/3140081718/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/3196819058","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82#issuecomment-3196819058","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82","id":3196819058,"node_id":"IC_kwDON056nM6-i5Zy","user":{"login":"tadasant","id":3900899,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDA4OTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3900899?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant","html_url":"https://github.com/tadasant","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tadasant/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-18T13:16:40Z","updated_at":"2025-08-18T13:16:40Z","body":"cc @joan-anthropic thought you might find this of interest as something DXT would want to see land","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/3196819058/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/3418662939","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82#issuecomment-3418662939","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82","id":3418662939,"node_id":"IC_kwDON056nM7LxKgb","user":{"login":"connor4312","id":2230985,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMzA5ODU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2230985?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312","html_url":"https://github.com/connor4312","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"created_at":"2025-10-18T17:01:21Z","updated_at":"2025-10-18T17:01:21Z","body":"This is an API I'm working on to have a VS Code extension version of the server manifest with static Tools declarations, to serve as possible inspiration: https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/issues/272000","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/3418662939/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/3799627826","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82#issuecomment-3799627826","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82","id":3799627826,"node_id":"IC_kwDON056nM7iebgy","user":{"login":"goncalossilva","id":102931,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMjkzMQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102931?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva","html_url":"https://github.com/goncalossilva","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goncalossilva/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T13:32:35Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T13:32:35Z","body":"As I started to work on adding tool definitions (including annotations) into registry/manifest so they can be discovered without starting/authing the server, I came across [SEP-1649](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/issues/1649) which tackles this too. Best of all, [it's already in review](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/pull/2127).","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/3799627826/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/4148381743","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82#issuecomment-4148381743","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82","id":4148381743,"node_id":"IC_kwDON056nM73Q0gv","user":{"login":"razashariff","id":36504271,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NTA0Mjcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36504271?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/razashariff","html_url":"https://github.com/razashariff","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/razashariff/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/razashariff/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/razashariff/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/razashariff/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/razashariff/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/razashariff/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/razashariff/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/razashariff/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/razashariff/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-28T16:31:34Z","updated_at":"2026-03-28T16:31:34Z","body":"Pre-registration security scanning would go a long way here. Every server submitted to the registry could be scanned for OWASP MCP Top 10 issues before listing.\n\nWe built [cybersecify](https://cybersecify.co.uk) for exactly this — 8 security tools that can scan any MCP server for auth bypass, command injection, SSRF, tool poisoning, rug pulls, unsigned messages, replay attacks, and rate limiting.\n\nA registry integration could work like:\n1. Server submitted for listing\n2. Automated `scan_server` runs the OWASP MCP Top 10 checks\n3. `assess_risk` scores every exposed tool\n4. Results displayed as a security badge on the listing\n\nWe also have [DVMCP](https://dvmcp.co.uk) as a test target — deliberately vulnerable, 10 intentional issues, useful for validating any scanning pipeline.\n\n`npx cybersecify` — zero dependencies, works today.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/4148381743/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/5385582407","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82#issuecomment-5385582407","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82","id":5385582407,"node_id":"IC_kwDON056nM8AAAABQQF3Rw","user":{"login":"DSHCorrectover","id":319894661,"node_id":"U_kgDOExE0hQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/319894661?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DSHCorrectover","html_url":"https://github.com/DSHCorrectover","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DSHCorrectover/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DSHCorrectover/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DSHCorrectover/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DSHCorrectover/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DSHCorrectover/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DSHCorrectover/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DSHCorrectover/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DSHCorrectover/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DSHCorrectover/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-23T10:42:57Z","updated_at":"2026-08-24T12:08:40Z","body":"Related finding from our work on signed MCP tool-call receipts: we caught a nested field injection attack class in our own proxy testing. A compromised upstream can inject forged signature/receipt fields at arbitrary nesting depths (3+ levels inside objects and arrays) in the JSON-RPC response. If verification only strips top-level keys or hashes before sanitizing, forged fields survive into any signed evidence.\n\nTwo implications for tool-call signatures:\n\n1. **Recursive sanitization before signing is non-negotiable.** Any reserved-prefix key (`_sig`, `_receipt`, `_verified`, etc.) must be stripped at ALL depths — in objects AND arrays — before hashing. Top-level-only stripping misses nested injection.\n\n2. **Order matters: strip → canonicalize → hash → sign.** If you hash before stripping, injected fields become part of the signed hash and you've cryptographically attested to attacker-controlled data.\n\nWe packaged detection as a standalone CLI (`npx ccs-lint --demo`, zero deps, 10KB, offline) that recursively scans MCP responses for injected fields at any depth and validates receipt structure. Test 17 covers 3-deep nested injection across both objects and arrays.\n\nTechnical write-up: https://dshcorrectover.github.io/ccs-proxy/blog/malicious-upstream.html\nnpm: https://www.npmjs.com/package/ccs-lint\n\nHappy to share the test cases if useful for the signature spec here.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/5385582407/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"spam"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/5714690074","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82#issuecomment-5714690074","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82","id":5714690074,"node_id":"IC_kwDON056nM8AAAABVJ9AGg","user":{"login":"qy6on","id":240369662,"node_id":"U_kgDODlO__g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240369662?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qy6on","html_url":"https://github.com/qy6on","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qy6on/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qy6on/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qy6on/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qy6on/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qy6on/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qy6on/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qy6on/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qy6on/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qy6on/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-17T12:54:46Z","updated_at":"2026-09-17T12:54:46Z","body":"Registry fingerprints and SEP-1649 answer \"what did this server declare when it was published\".\nThere's a second half that a registry structurally cannot cover: **what the server served *you*, in\n*this* session.**\n\nA server can pass pre-registration scanning and still hand a specific client a different tool\ndefinition at `tools/list` time — different description, different schema, different annotations.\nThe registry never sees that exchange, so a publication-time fingerprint can't witness it. That is\nalso the shape of the rug pull: the definition that gets approved and the definition that is later\nserved are not the same object.\n\nThe client-side half is cheap and needs no registry cooperation: digest each tool's name,\ndescription, input schema and annotations at listing time, keep a manifest digest of the set, and\ncompare on every subsequent listing. A changed definition is then detectable in-session, and if the\ndigests go into a hash-linked record, provable afterwards. The two compose — a registry fingerprint\ngives you an expected value, and the client-side digest tells you whether what arrived matches it.\n\nOn @DSHCorrectover's nested field injection: computing the digest over an **extracted, fixed field\nset** rather than over the raw JSON-RPC response closes that class by construction. Fields injected\nat any nesting depth are simply not inputs to the digest, so they cannot alter or forge it. It costs\nyou detection of the injected fields themselves, which is a separate check, but the evidence value\nof the digest survives a compromised upstream.\n\nI've implemented the client-side half in [infy](https://github.com/Infyrence/infy) (Apache-2.0) as a\nwrapper around `mcp.ClientSession`, tested end-to-end against a live server including a real\nmid-session description rewrite. Happy to write it up as a client-side recommendation here if that's\nuseful to the SEP-1649 discussion.\n\nOne related thing worth stating in this thread regardless: `ToolAnnotations` are unverified server\nclaims, and the SDK says so — *\"clients should never make tool use decisions based on ToolAnnotations\nreceived from untrusted servers.\"* If annotations get carried into registry manifests for\ndiscovery-without-connecting, that caveat needs to travel with them, or a `readOnlyHint` becomes a\ntrust signal purely by virtue of being in a registry.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/5714690074/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/5851975202","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82#issuecomment-5851975202","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82","id":5851975202,"node_id":"IC_kwDON056nM8AAAABXM4OIg","user":{"login":"gostanos","id":232411410,"node_id":"U_kgDODdpREg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/232411410?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gostanos","html_url":"https://github.com/gostanos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gostanos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gostanos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gostanos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gostanos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gostanos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gostanos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gostanos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gostanos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gostanos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-27T02:30:04Z","updated_at":"2026-09-27T02:33:31Z","body":"Building on the last comment: there's a third thing between those two, which is what each *release* of a server declared, over time.\n\nI run smallprint.dev, which reads the published tool definitions of the servers in this registry (plus npm and PyPI) every night and keeps a hash per version over every tool's name, description and input schema. That way you can see when a description changed between releases, and diff it.\n\nOn the client side, `npx smallprint check --locked` compares what's installed on your machine against a lock you took earlier, and fails when a tool changed.\n\nIt doesn't cover the per-session case qy6on describes, a server that serves one client something different at `tools/list`. That needs a check in the client itself.\n\nThe per-version digests are public, one server at a time, for example https://smallprint.dev/api/receipt/npm/@ai-sdk/mcp/2.0.49\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/5851975202/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/6375359997","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82#issuecomment-6375359997","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82","id":6375359997,"node_id":"IC_kwDON056nM8AAAABfABF_Q","user":{"login":"rdimitrov","id":16540482,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTQwNDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16540482?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdimitrov","html_url":"https://github.com/rdimitrov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdimitrov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdimitrov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdimitrov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdimitrov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdimitrov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdimitrov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdimitrov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdimitrov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdimitrov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-23T21:44:52Z","updated_at":"2026-10-23T21:44:52Z","body":"Consolidating two related tool-surface proposals into this tracker:\n\n- #1681 proposes links to externally observed tool-change history, keyed by server/version plus canonical tool-surface digest, observation time and observer identity.\n- #1720 proposes an optional publisher-attested `surfaceHash` with explicit canonicalization and a reference format/implementation.\n\nKeep the distinction between publisher declarations and third-party observations. The design still needs canonicalization rules, treatment of annotations and dynamic/auth-dependent tools, and client verification semantics; closing the parallel proposal threads does not adopt a format or imply that this has been implemented. Their source links and evidence remain in the linked issues.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/6375359997/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":1144995,"client_id":"Iv23liVemv8A9if9v0F2","slug":"chatgpt-codex-connector","node_id":"A_kwHOAOQ6Gs4AEXij","owner":{"login":"openai","id":14957082,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjE0OTU3MDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14957082?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai","html_url":"https://github.com/openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"ChatGPT Codex Connector","description":"Bring ChatGPT and Codex to your GitHub repositories.","external_url":"https://www.chatgpt.com","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/chatgpt-codex-connector","created_at":"2025-02-14T01:37:05Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T18:52:59Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","checks":"read","contents":"write","emails":"read","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"read","workflows":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","commit_comment","issues","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","repository","status","sub_issues"]},"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/6377409983","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82#issuecomment-6377409983","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82","id":6377409983,"node_id":"IC_kwDON056nM8AAAABfB-Nvw","user":{"login":"gostanos","id":232411410,"node_id":"U_kgDODdpREg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/232411410?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gostanos","html_url":"https://github.com/gostanos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gostanos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gostanos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gostanos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gostanos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gostanos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gostanos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gostanos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gostanos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gostanos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-24T00:18:18Z","updated_at":"2026-10-24T00:18:18Z","body":"@rdimitrov\n\n> The design still needs canonicalization rules, treatment of annotations and dynamic/auth-dependent tools, and client verification semantics\n\nHere's how those came out in practice for smallprint.dev, as one data point.\n\nCanonical form: JSON of [{name, description, inputSchema}] sorted by tool name, with every object key sorted recursively. Prose (the name, the description, and any description or title inside the schema) gets runs of whitespace collapsed to one space and trimmed. Every other string (enum, const, pattern, default) stays byte for byte since whitespace can mean something there, and `required` arrays get sorted because their order doesn't. Prose over 20,000 characters goes in as its opening plus the length and SHA-256 of the whole, so the digest still covers every character. The digest is SHA-256 of that JSON.\n\nAnnotations, title and outputSchema aren't in that digest. Whether they belong in a shared format is one of the calls this thread would have to make.\n\nDynamic and auth-gated tools: an observer like mine only sees what a server lists without credentials. It reads the published package, and where it can't, it starts the package in a container with no network and no keys, so anything that only shows up after sign-in isn't in the digest. The record keeps how each version was read, and I think an observation format should carry that too.\n\nVerification: each version's line goes into a daily row, the rows are hash-chained and signed with Ed25519, and the public key is published. The receipt for a version gives the digest, when it was recorded and the row that holds it, and a short public script recomputes everything from the API. That's the observation time and observer identity #1681 asks for, and a changed or deleted observation would show up as a broken chain.\n\nExample, the one from my last comment: https://smallprint.dev/api/receipt/npm/@ai-sdk/mcp/2.0.49 (the script is https://github.com/gostanos/smallprint-action/blob/main/tools/verify-chain.mjs)\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/6377409983/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/6388128394","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82#issuecomment-6388128394","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82","id":6388128394,"node_id":"IC_kwDON056nM8AAAABfMMaig","user":{"login":"Paraphern","id":297951147,"node_id":"U_kgDOEcJfqw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297951147?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Paraphern","html_url":"https://github.com/Paraphern","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Paraphern/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Paraphern/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Paraphern/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Paraphern/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Paraphern/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Paraphern/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Paraphern/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Paraphern/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Paraphern/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-24T18:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-10-24T18:47:27Z","body":"Following the consolidation from #1720 — contributing working answers to the four open questions, from a spec that's implemented and running (PIN-SPEC, plus a live cross-implementation check below).\n\n**Canonicalization:** RFC 8785 (JCS) profile — recursive key sort, compact serialization, non-ASCII as raw UTF-8, numbers per JCS §3.2.2.3. The one rule worth naming explicitly: both sides must state their float serialization, because it's unexercised until a schema carries a non-integer number — in a live cross-implementation check (our `surfaceHash` vs an external observatory's `manifest_hash` over the same public endpoint's capture, [rugsnare#6](https://github.com/Paraphern/rugsnare/issues/6)) the digests agreed byte-for-byte, with the float case explicitly called out as the open edge rather than assumed compatible.\n\n**Annotations:** store, never hash, compare spec-default-aware — an absent hint equals the spec default, so appearance and disappearance both count as changes. We grade a flipped behavioral hint (`readOnlyHint` etc.) as its own finding class, separate from schema drift; that separation has held up in practice.\n\n**Verification semantics:** publisher-attested fingerprints want receipts, not just fields — Ed25519-signed pins, so \"the publisher approved this surface\" is attributable and tamper-evident in the registry entry itself.\n\n**Dynamic/auth-dependent tools:** a surface captured under one auth context is a *different surface* — the fingerprint should name its capture context (unauthenticated prober vs authenticated client), which is precisely the publisher-attested vs externally-observed distinction this thread preserved from #1720. Two hashes on one entry, each labeled with its vantage, joins cleanly later.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/6388128394/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/6711079035","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82#issuecomment-6711079035","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82","id":6711079035,"node_id":"IC_kwDON056nM8AAAABkALwew","user":{"login":"emmanuelorta","id":253105980,"node_id":"U_kgDODxYXPA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/253105980?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta","html_url":"https://github.com/emmanuelorta","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-07T18:05:19Z","updated_at":"2026-11-07T18:05:19Z","body":"On the open question of canonicalization and annotations (rdimitrov's consolidation note), here is a cross-check of three public observers on the same servers, the same day.\n\n**Method.** On 2026-11-07 between 17:16 and 17:18 UTC, I read `tools/list` live once from 30 registry remotes (479 tools, all pages, chosen at random from servers that HISTOR, heldfast and CrawlCheck all record), plus CrawlCheck's own server. To those bytes I applied each project's documented digest:\n- **HISTOR MTL/1:** `{name, description, inputSchema, outputSchema?}`, one RFC 8785 array sorted by name in UTF-16 code-unit order, SRI.\n- **heldfast:** per tool only, over `{name, title, description, input_schema, annotations, output_schema?, icons?}` with `\"\"`/`{}` defaults, RFC 8785, hex.\n- **CrawlCheck lockfile v1** (I work on it): `{name, description, inputSchema, annotations}`, nulls for absent fields; the list hash is the sorted per-tool hashes joined by `\\n`.\n\n**Result.**\n- 30/30: MTL/1 over my bytes equals HISTOR's published `toolSetDigest`.\n- 30/30: heldfast's per-tool digest over my bytes equals every tool in its feed `state/` file (479/479 tools).\n- 30/30: CrawlCheck's live `POST /api/v1/mcp/lock` equals its spec.\n- 0/30: any digest can be compared across projects.\n\nSo the observations agree. Only the field scope and the list-hash construction differ. Of the 30 servers, 18 send `title`/`annotations`, 4 send `outputSchema`, 8 send `execution` and 5 send `_meta`. Any of these moves one project's digest and not another's.\n\nA sample (reproduce from `https://histor.modelmarket.dev/api/v1/servers?q=<name>` and `rufat325/heldfast-feed/state/remote__<name>.json`):\n\n| server | tools | HISTOR toolSetDigest | MTL/1 of live bytes | heldfast tools equal | CrawlCheck lk v1 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| io.github.emmanuelorta/crawlcheck | 27 | `sha256-AxcAxfuTrbxxTMqG80WqtRmiGfO4kaoqWJDBCooXSDg=` | same | 27/27 | `033775e1e9b87637…` |\n| com.focxle/afos | 58 | `sha256-V2su5xHuYY2wBDtyEcMHOM0DKKLyydTE37u7lt81O5A=` | same | 58/58 | `846dcfeea10816ba…` |\n| io.github.eorscope/eorscope-mcp | 14 (sends outputSchema, annotations, _meta) | `sha256-2KGyt6Dq9U9Sv28QPOUa64x0tR5Hi4vjhN1jbW/XEa8=` | same | 14/14 | `305f725ab2e3fc51…` |\n\n**What would make these comparable without anyone re-hashing their history:**\n1. **RFC 8785, SHA-256.** Numbers as ECMAScript writes them; keys in UTF-16 code-unit order. A missing name, a number with no double, or a partially paginated list yields no digest (null plus a reason).\n2. **Two digests per tool.**\n   - `contract` = `{name, description, inputSchema, outputSchema?}`.\n   - `extras` = `{title?, annotations?, icons?}`.\n   - `_meta` is in neither.\n   - The list-level `contract_set` is exactly MTL/1's tool-set digest. It already matched on 30/30, so adopting it moves no published value.\n   - `extras_set` is the same construction over `[{name, extras}]`.\n3. **Material change classes**, so an annotation edit is neither hidden nor reported as a rug pull:\n   - removed, added, description rewritten, schema widened;\n   - hint escalated: `readOnlyHint` true→false/absent, `destructiveHint` or `openWorldHint` →true, absent hints compared as spec defaults;\n   - cosmetic: title or icons only.\n4. **Version expectation.** A `contract_set` change or a hint escalation SHOULD come with a new `serverInfo.version`; observers record `version_unchanged: true` when it does not. (HISTOR's record of my own server shows seven tool-set changes since 10-10, each at an unchanged `serverInfo.version`. The version was bumped to 1.2.0 only afterwards. That is how I found this.)\n5. **Change event.** A JCS-signed object with registry name, endpoint, versions before and after, both digests before and after, per-tool classes, and observer id plus vantage (unauthenticated vs publisher, per #1720). Observers that agree on `after.contract_set` corroborate one another without sharing code.\n\nCrawlCheck now publishes this alongside its old hash, without changing the old one: `jcs_v1` in lockfiles and in `/api/v1/mcp/changes`, documented with test vectors at https://crawlcheck.io/spec/mcp-lockfile#jcs-v1. Its value for the server above is `sha256-AxcAxfuTrbxxTMqG80WqtRmiGfO4kaoqWJDBCooXSDg=`, the same as HISTOR's. The 30-server table and the script are available if anyone wants to re-run them.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/6711079035/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/6711311079","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82#issuecomment-6711311079","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82","id":6711311079,"node_id":"IC_kwDON056nM8AAAABkAZ65w","user":{"login":"emmanuelorta","id":253105980,"node_id":"U_kgDODxYXPA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/253105980?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta","html_url":"https://github.com/emmanuelorta","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelorta/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-07T18:26:04Z","updated_at":"2026-11-07T18:26:04Z","body":"Correction to point 2 above, on `extras`. HISTOR already publishes `toolExtrasDigest`, and its construction differs from what I wrote. It covers every tool member except `name`, `description`, `inputSchema` and `outputSchema` (so `title`, `annotations`, `icons`, `execution`, `_meta` and vendor fields), as `{\"tools\": {<name>: <extras>}}`. CrawlCheck's `jcs_v1.extras_sha256` now uses that scope with RFC 8785 and equals HISTOR's published `toolExtrasDigest` on the same 30 servers: 30/30, including the 10 with no extras. For io.github.emmanuelorta/crawlcheck both are `sha256-G44DGgW7+rp9YjMAaEG80Tm5RFoke8eYkrE6nGk69y8=`.\n\nThe two encodings can still differ in three narrow cases: astral-plane characters in tool names (sort order), integral floats such as `1.0`, and integers beyond 2^53. Worth settling if this becomes the shared definition. Spec and test vector: https://crawlcheck.io/spec/mcp-lockfile#jcs-v1\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/6711311079/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/6711424834","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82#issuecomment-6711424834","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/82","id":6711424834,"node_id":"IC_kwDON056nM8AAAABkAg3Qg","user":{"login":"Paraphern","id":297951147,"node_id":"U_kgDOEcJfqw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297951147?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Paraphern","html_url":"https://github.com/Paraphern","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Paraphern/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Paraphern/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Paraphern/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Paraphern/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Paraphern/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Paraphern/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Paraphern/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Paraphern/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Paraphern/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-07T18:36:21Z","updated_at":"2026-11-07T18:36:21Z","body":"Following up on our earlier canonicalization answer: the pin-then-verify loop is now complete end-to-end. As of rugsnare 1.6.0 (on npm today), the Ed25519-signed pin store is checked **before the server starts** (tampered baseline = boot-time failure), and in enforce mode, individual tools whose contracts drifted are **blocked at call time** — not just flagged after the fact.\n\nField data unchanged: 218 silent changes in the npm ecosystem, 140 across reference servers. A `fingerprints` field in the registry spec would give clients a pre-approval baseline to diff against; we'd adopt it on day one.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/registry/issues/comments/6711424834/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]